  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bus company Sulaymaniyah</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled because of the lack of progress and no chances for improving that situation.The regional government of Northern Iraq is setting steps to improve public transport. The applicant, Fijen, to make life easier B.V., is discussing the subject already for some years with the authorities and involved the public transport company of Amsterdam (GVB) in the discussions. This resulted in the idea to set up a pilot for a bus line in Sulaymaniyah.The intended pilot will create a bus line that runs from points at feeder roads of the city and runs for approximately twenty kilometres through the centre of the city.The applicant is active in manufacturing and distribution of safety provisions for roads and vehicles. The local partner is WHAR Group Contracting and General Trading Ltd., a contracting company. GVB will be involved in the implementation, though not as an official partner but as subcontractor. The partners will set up a joint venture for the company.The project will introduce public bus transport on an organised level in the municipality of Sulaymaniyah and in that way will reduce the traffic jams in the city.</narrative>
  </description>
